        }
      ],
      "id": "cpn55dt"
    },
    {
      "id": "0hci1ud",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning and Importance of DPSP"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP) establish guidelines for governance and policy formulation.",
        "DPSPs are broadly classified into Socialist, Gandhian, and Liberal–Intellectual Principles.",
        "A core conceptual requirement is understanding the specific Articles related to DPSP.",
        "Distinguishing between Fundamental Rights and DPSP is essential for constitutional clarity."
      ],
      "id": "mo792k9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "syek9v2",
      "content": "• DPSP aim to establish social and economic democracy in India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vxsjbj1",
      "content": "• They guide the government in making laws and policies."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k4cnxjy",
      "content": "• They promote welfare of the people."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rlx568y",
      "content": "• They help in establishing a welfare state."
    },
    {
